              ],
              "content": "Fig. 2.7"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_13_image_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.108,
            0.81,
            0.891,
            0.854
          ],
          "content": "**Example 14:** Draw the graphs of $y=\\frac{1}{2}x,y=x,y=2x$ by selecting suitable points on these lines."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.107,
            0.858,
            0.889,
            0.91
          ],
          "content": "(**Hint:** In order to graph $y \\; = \\; { \\frac { 1 } { 2 } } \\; x ,$ we could take the points (0, 0) and (4, 2). Can you verify that these lie on the line?)"
        }
      ]
    }
